                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aad80071-f733-31c2-8fd1-ce815a401131",
                        "entry_id": "e423a25b-bc3f-3463-9d15-1fa0dd34b28c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sufficiency (of a statement, claim etc.) to carry weight in law; legal pertinence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Scotland",
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7ebf6b6-c6ef-350f-adc7-ccfcbd029868",
                        "entry_id": "e423a25b-bc3f-3463-9d15-1fa0dd34b28c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The degree to which a thing is relevant; relevance, applicability."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4c49abc1-0e2b-477a-bfcc-8d194133beba",
                                "sense_id": "e7ebf6b6-c6ef-350f-adc7-ccfcbd029868",
                                "text": "It is the malpractice of the courts to confine evidence and discussion to the bounds of apparent relevancy."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4e9be115-1998-3746-920f-a16d209543d3",
                        "entry_id": "e423a25b-bc3f-3463-9d15-1fa0dd34b28c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A relevant thing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d01c8eb9-7a7b-44f7-85c7-58ab5cde6f25",
                                "sense_id": "4e9be115-1998-3746-920f-a16d209543d3",
                                "text": "To believe that such talk really ever came out of people's mouths would be to believe that there was a time when time was of no value to a person who thought he had something to say; when it was the custom to spread a two-minute remark out to ten; when a man's mouth was a rolling-mill, and busied itself all day long in turning four-foot pigs of thought into thirty-foot bars of conversational railroad iron by attenuation; when subjects were seldom faithfully stuck to, but the talk wandered all around and arrived nowhere; when conversations consisted mainly of irrelevancies, with here and there a relevancy, a relevancy with an embarrassed look, as not being able to explain how it got there."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3750daac-abf8-42d0-8a60-4b41f36e372b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e423a25b-bc3f-3463-9d15-1fa0dd34b28c",
                        "source_sense_description": "the degrees to which a thing is relevant",
                        "target_lang_word": "pertinence",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pertinence",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8c2e33f7-68ae-384e-8322-50b57d916e51",
                                        "entry_id": "ded77db7-26e3-3045-bf09-0a223222d0ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualité de ce qui est pertinent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d5a10b0-a034-4861-a8b4-86e35953fe09",
                                                "sense_id": "8c2e33f7-68ae-384e-8322-50b57d916e51",
                                                "text": "En cas de doute sur la pertinence de l'exorcisme, mieux vaut alors faire appel aux chérifs détenteurs d'une baraka reconnue pour sa puissance thérapeutique."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ff7ed1a-117a-4066-b121-56a5b4181a5c",
                                                "sense_id": "8c2e33f7-68ae-384e-8322-50b57d916e51",
                                                "text": "Chacun de nous put acquérir pour une modique somme une K7 contant le reportage et vingt minutes de rush qu'il eut la gentillesse de rendre intelligentes, ce qui dut lui donner beaucoup de mal, car, honnêtement, nos déplacements rugbystiques n'ont jamais vraiment brillé ni par leur originalité, ni par la pertinence de nos pensées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c01e0e4-a66f-4146-b702-3532c102fc8e",
                                                "sense_id": "8c2e33f7-68ae-384e-8322-50b57d916e51",
                                                "text": "L'origine onomatopéique d'un lexème est une question diachronique, sans pertinence en tant que telle pour la sémantique de la parole : ainsi, il n'est pas fondamental pour nous de trancher parmi les nombreux cas qui peuvent faire débats (quid de gong, flaque, grogner, grommeler, siffler, claquer, vrombir... ?)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
